Third-party software distributed in the container image
-------------------------------------------------------

The lftpweb container image bundles unmodified third-party programs from the Alpine
Linux package repositories. They are aggregated with lftpweb, not derived from it or
linked into it — lftpweb invokes them as separate processes — so each remains under
its own licence:

  lftp             GPL-3.0-or-later   https://lftp.yar.ru/
  openssh-client   BSD-style          https://www.openssh.com/
  7zip (7zz)       LGPL-2.1-or-later, with the unRAR restriction applying to its
                   RAR decoding code   https://www.7-zip.org/
  su-exec          MIT                https://github.com/ncopa/su-exec
  tini             MIT                https://github.com/krallin/tini

Complete corresponding source for these packages is available from the Alpine Linux
project at https://pkgs.alpinelinux.org/ — the image ships them unmodified, exactly as
packaged there.

Note on lftp: lftpweb runs lftp as a subprocess and communicates with it at arm's
length. It does not link against lftp, and is not a derivative work of it.

Note on 7zip's RAR support: 7-Zip's RAR decoder derives from the unRAR source, whose
licence forbids using it to develop a RAR-compatible archiver. lftpweb only extracts
archives; it never creates them.
